From 07a2dbd15f694d2ac1623d567b67aff311b45929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Troy Mitchell <troy.mitchell@linux.spacemit.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:23:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 200/468] FROMLIST: riscv: dts: spacemit: k3-com260-ifx: Drop
 wrong SD card vmmc-supply

The SD card VDD on the K3 CoM260 module comes from a fixed, always-on
3.3 V rail that software cannot control. ALDO4 of the P1 PMIC does not
supply the card, so referencing it as vmmc-supply describes the wrong
power wiring.

Drop the vmmc-supply property. It is optional for a card powered by a
fixed supply, and the SDHCI core then uses the voltages advertised by
the controller.

Fixes: 055044260e7a ("riscv: dts: spacemit: k3: Enable SD card support")
Signed-off-by: Troy Mitchell <troy.mitchell@linux.spacemit.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261105-k3-com260-module-sd-nor-mac-v1-1-138b39d74602@linux.spacemit.com
Signed-off-by: Han Gao <gaohan@iscas.ac.cn>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts
index 6eb4a5ad073c5..ab272fbf75ac4 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts
@@ -194,7 +194,6 @@ &sdhci0 {
 	no-sdio;
 	disable-wp;
 	cap-sd-highspeed;
-	vmmc-supply = <&aldo4>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&aldo1>;
 	sd-uhs-sdr25;
 	sd-uhs-sdr50;
-- 
